Interpretation of price deltas
- Before the additional poltrona reclassification, explicit-price baseline counts were ASR 59/85 and reference 64/85 (L7 checkpoint). Re-routing MP-0004, MP-0062, MP-0067 to OTRO with ORIGINAL git-base code makes their explicit 5,500 amounts visible in the baseline (all three were missing in old MUEBLE_MEDIDA ASR results). Thus the resulting baseline moves to 62/85 ASR and 67/85 reference: a corpus-routing effect, not an NLP improvement.
- Against that correctly routed baseline, after-v5 improves to 65/85 ASR and 70/85 reference. The three before->after price-field gains are MP-0005/MP-0063/MP-0068 (the earlier price-per-game fix), not the newly added numeric-name rule.

Independent new-rule probe outcomes
- Fresh scratch baseline is `git archive c94e7a8`; candidate is current `src/`. Actual frozen ASR inputs for MP-0004/0062: baseline fields only price_lista=5500.00; candidate adds literal name `2 poltronas fijas` and observations exactly equal to complete ASR text, retains price 5500.00, adds neither cantidad nor unidad_stock, and emits no chair-only fields. MP-0067 already started with words “Dos poltronas”; baseline and candidate fields are identical (full name/observations and 5500.00).
- Synthetic `2 poltronas fijas…` candidate: nombre exactly retains numeric literal; full observations exact; price 5500.00; keys only nombre/observaciones/precio_lista. Word-count natural name and `Producto: 2 poltronas fijas…` labeled equivalent are byte/semantic equal baseline vs candidate.
- Dimensions/currency-only starts, zero, negative, decimal counts, negation, and admin starts create no new name; baseline and candidate outputs equal for these forms. One odd administrative phrase `Precio unitario de 2 poltronas fijas` still returns `precio_lista=2.00` without name in both baseline and candidate; pre-existing and unchanged.
- Legacy CLI forms “Dos mesas. Precio unitario 250 bolivianos.” (BOB and USD), “Un escritorio de melamina con cajones.”, “Un closet de dos puertas.”, and “Un mueble con casilleros” all exit 0, empty stderr, and identical JSON after removing only timing.
